{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789301180,"nonce":"SzDTo6MSiVd/wlnBCV2pjS9UpYA=","message":"Landed on main as 0879e97be9091a83ed62a1c9ab0f26f972eecf67 (fast-forward; the owner's in-flight AIR edits\nare disjoint and untouched). crates/ash/src/host_module.rs: HostModule\ndescription, register_host_module, JSON seam export in ash_core (ash_std\ncannot see DecodedBytecode). Resolver: with_host_natives publishes to a\nprocess-global host registry and the symbol table, consulted before std\nand HDLLs; discover_and_load_libraries skips fully host-covered libs.\nClass objects: init_host_classes after init_constants. 68 core unit\ntests; e2e in interp, hybrid and jit modes with stdout 3; parity 120/120.\n\nTwo HashLink facts the host must follow: genhl emits no target for\n@:hlNative on an instance method, so the binding shape is a static\nnative taking the receiver wrapped by an inline instance method (the\nfixture and HashLink's own std do this); and extern class is refused by\nthe HL target, so a macro-emitted class always puts the type in the\nprogram. Consequence: a host class with the same name as a program class\nis currently an error, so the real flow registers a host-only companion\n(e.g. host.Greeters) and the program's natives bind by (lib, name).\n\nOpen: a \"bind to the program's existing class and verify\" registration\nmode for the same-named case; Type.resolveClass cannot see host\nclasses; hot reload re-decodes from disk and drops registrations.","files":null}]}